.nh
.TH "PB-DOCTOR" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-doctor - Check Paperboat connectivity and readiness


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb doctor [machine] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Check authentication, the local runtime and connectivity for this machine, or for one
machine you name. Without --repair the command only reports findings and how to recover; --repair
performs the supported local fixes (on Windows it includes a privileged step). Exit status is 0
when everything is healthy and 1 otherwise, so scripts should use --json and the exit status.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for doctor

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--repair\fP[=false]
	repair Paperboat-owned local dependencies (Windows) and restart the local daemon, then check


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb doctor
  pb doctor studio --json
  pb doctor --repair
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP
